  "operative_text": "Section 1 (KRS 237.109): (1) Persons age eighteen (18) or older, and otherwise able to lawfully possess a firearm, may carry concealed firearms or other concealed deadly weapons without a license in the same locations as persons with valid licenses issued under KRS 237.110.\nSection 1 (KRS 237.109): (2) This section shall not be construed to allow the carrying or possession of any deadly weapon where it is prohibited by federal law.\nSection 2 (KRS 237.110): (c) Is eighteen (18) years of age or older;"
